From c47575b59b828171f6f8355e827d1f138975ade6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JimmyBlunt <jo@paso-music.de>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:14:23 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] Ausgabe deck section: per-Pattern Helligkeit, Speed,
 Hue, Scale, Rotate that reach the router (local #9002)

Every Pattern (Pixelblaze and FastLED) gets a deck section "Ausgabe" whose
values act on the frame the router receives as well as the preview:
Helligkeit and Hue adjust the finished RGB frame (before the active mask),
Speed is the one time factor (Pixelblaze delta and the FastLED virtual
clock; the Preview speed dropdown is gone), Scale/Rotate move the sampled
map coordinates (Pixelblaze) or the FastLED surface projection's fit
(greyed out for the index projection). The sun slider stays a monitor-only
brightness. Neutral values are bit-identical (Fast/Precise, FastLED L1/L2).

Values are per-pattern cascaded settings (PatternRecord.settings or
demoOverrides), seeded before the first router frame, and a demo's router
frames wait for its persisted overrides. Zuruecksetzen drops just the five
fields. Nothing reaches a Controller push.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
