@@ -445,6 +445,7 @@ A FastLED Pattern is detected by `patternLanguage(src)` (`src/engine/patternLang
 - Preview: `Preview.tsx` resolves the layout with the `@pxlblz-dim` dimension, passes `PXLBLZ_NUM_LEDS` (and `PXLBLZ_WIDTH/HEIGHT` for regular grids), runs the vendored host (`src/engine/fastled/fastledWasmHost.ts`, ABI 1) in a Web Worker (`fastled.worker.ts` → `fastledWorkerCore.ts`, main side `FastLedWorkerHost`, `?fastledWorker=0` = main thread) and drives `createFastLedPatternHandle` through the shared `startLoop` (fast shim always). `beforeRender(dt)` runs `frame(dt)`; `render*(i)` emits byte/255 of L2 wire bytes (default, RGB order after brightness/correction/dither) or L1 `leds[]`. byte/255 → `Math.round(v*255)` is exact, so the packed frame and the router receive FastLED's bytes (golden test: 0 differing bytes against the native FastLED reference).
 - Projection (`src/engine/fastled/fastledProjection.ts`, deck section "FastLED" in `FastLedProjectionPanel.tsx`): *index* keeps `leds[i]` → map index i and passes `PXLBLZ_NUM_LEDS` = map pixel count; *surface* compiles without PXLBLZ defines (the sketch keeps its NUM_LEDS) and gives the handle a precomputed table map index → sketch LED (−1 = black), so `render*(i)` emits the L2/L1 bytes of `table[i]` and the packed frame keeps the map's pixel count (router frame size unchanged). Sketch positions: the sketch's screen maps (`getScreenMaps()`, host export `pxl_screenmap_json`, sent by the worker with `started`/changed frames; serpentine/XYMap already applied), else the catalogue `geometry` width×height row-major (serpentine when the source declares `kMatrixSerpentineLayout = true`/`SERPENTINE true`; a clone finds its example by the provenance header), else a square guess with a deck notice. Map positions: each pixel's `sample` (2D: x,y; 3D: chosen axis pair, default the two largest extents), fitted onto the sketch bounds padded by half an LED (Contain: uniform scale, whole map inside the sketch; Fill: per axis), optional flips; nearest sketch LED within one LED pitch via a bucket grid, ties → lower index; memoised per (map points, sketch layout, options), ~ms for 10,330 pixels. Automatic choice: surface for `@pxlblz-dim` ≥ 2 on a ≥2D map unless the source uses `PXLBLZ_NUM_LEDS/WIDTH/HEIGHT` or the known LED count (catalogue, or after start) equals the map's. Persistence: `// @pxlblz-projection [index|surface] [fit=fill] [flip=x|y|xy] [axes=xy|xz|yz]` in an editable Pattern's header; the compile request blanks that line and the artifact cache key drops it, so a projection change never recompiles. Read-only examples store the same text as `fastledProjection` in their `demoOverrides` bag (cleared by "Revert to recommended"); Clone writes it into the copy's header.
 - Active mask (`src/engine/maps/activeMask.ts`, all Patterns, not only FastLED): a custom map record may carry `importMetadata.activeMask = { version: 1, encoding: 'rle01', count, first, runs, active, source?, fingerprint?, updatedAt? }` — alternating run lengths starting with value `first`, summing to `count`; `active` and `fingerprint` (`fnv1a32:` over the 0/1 bytes) are checked on decode. Stored in the existing `import_metadata_json` column (no migration; `PATCH /api/maps/:id` already writes `importMetadata` as a whole). A map whose metadata has no Controller provenance uses `kind: 'installation'`; only `kind: 'controller'` (`isControllerMapImport`) makes a map frozen or shows the "Imported" facts. `mapFromRecord` validates the mask against the point count (wrong length or malformed → ignored, `console.warn` and an amber deck/map-pane warning) and puts it on the `PixelMap`; `resolveLayout` returns `activeMask` (per pixel index, active past the baked array, null when nothing is masked) plus the summary. `createRenderLoop({ activeMask })` still calls `render*` for every index (Pattern state and determinism unchanged) and writes black for masked indices into the packed frame / pixel list, so preview and `externalPixelOutput` (router) get black there and unchanged bytes elsewhere. `Preview.tsx` hands the renderer only the active indices (positions, normals, and a compacted copy of each frame), so the parked cluster is neither drawn nor part of the measured bounds/spacing. The FastLED surface table gets `active`: masked points → −1 and excluded from the map bounds (Contain/Fill fit only real LED positions) and from the automatic 3D axis choice. Deck: "Maske: 6.962 aktiv / 3.368 ausgeblendet" (`editorStore.activeMaskLabel`); map pane fact row "Maske". Set/clear a mask with `node scripts/set-map-active-mask.mjs --map <id> --mask <0/1 JSON array>` (local dev session, merges with existing metadata, verifies after writing). Not applied yet: Shows, Gallery thumbnails, Controller (hardware) export.
+- Ausgabe (`src/engine/outputAdjust.ts`, deck section "Ausgabe" in `OutputPanel.tsx`, all Patterns, not only FastLED): five per-Pattern controls that reach the router. Settings fields (per-pattern cascaded, `settings.ts`): `outputBrightness` 0..1, `speed` 0..4 (the existing field; the Preview section's speed dropdown is gone, a stored value above 4 clamps to 4 on seed), `outputHue` −180..180°, `outputScale` 0.25..4, `outputRotate` −180..180°. Layer 1 lives where every other preview override lives: `PatternRecord.settings` (`settings_json`, no migration) for a personal Pattern, `demoOverrides` for a read-only demo / FastLED example; forks copy them like the rest. Chain: Speed scales the frame delta (`renderLoop` `getSpeed`: Pixelblaze `delta`/`time()` and the FastLED virtual clock, i.e. `frame(dt)` to the worker; 0 = frozen), Scale/Rotate move the map coordinates before the Pattern's own transform stack (`createRenderLoop({ getOutput })` → `transformMapCoordinates`: `c + R(−θ)·(p − c)/scale` about the bounding-box centre of the active samples, so the image turns by +θ from +x towards +y; 1D maps zoom x only and have no rotation; 3D maps rotate in the plane of the two largest extents, the plane `largestExtentAxes` gives the FastLED surface projection; for FastLED the loop leaves coordinates alone (`coordinateOutput: false`) and the surface table applies `zoom`/`rotateDeg` to the map positions before flips and fit, swapped live via the handle's `setProjection`; the index projection has no geometry, so the deck greys Scale/Rotate out), then on the finished frame Hue (HSV rotation, keeps max/min channel) → Helligkeit (multiply) → masked pixels stay black → renderer (times the preview-only monitor `brightness`) and `externalPixelOutput`. At neutral values (1, 1, 0°, 1, 0°) nothing is computed and frames are bit-identical (Pixelblaze Fast/Precise, FastLED L1/L2 goldens). The preview-only `brightness` (sun slider) stays a monitor control; it never reaches the router. Before the first frame of a newly opened Pattern, `startLoop` calls `ensureOutputSettingsSeeded()` (the open-time seed effect runs after the build effect); a demo's router frames are held back until `demoOverridesLoaded` so a persisted Helligkeit cannot flash at 100 %. "Zurücksetzen" drops the five fields from the layer-1 bag (`clearPatternSettingsFields` / `clearDemoSettingsFields`). Nothing of this is in pushed code (Send to Controller bundles the source; its JPEG thumbnail renders separately); Shows and static Gallery thumbnails ignore it.
 - Preview start: the deck pauses itself while no Pattern is loaded (upstream #478); it now resumes when the pause was automatic and a Pattern arrives (cold load, deep link), while a user pause stays.
 - Controls: FastLED UI elements map to ranged slider/toggle Controls (`PatternMetadata.controls[].range`); values persist in `PatternRecord.controls` (`controls_json`) keyed by UI name.
 - Worker and watchdog: the worker runs the same host calls in the same order, so bytes are identical; frames are pipelined by one IDE frame (frame(dt_k) requests frame k while frame k-1 is shown; a late answer repeats the last frame and the deltas accumulate). No answer within 2 s (setup 10 s) terminates the worker: runtime error, last frame kept. The host's loop/show budget still reports runaway loops that call `millis/delay/show` (they keep running). Measured at 4,593 LEDs: ~1 ms per frame in the worker, ~1.4 ms round trip, main-thread cost ~0.1 ms per frame; added latency one IDE frame.
